{"resultsPerPage":3,"startIndex":0,"totalResults":3,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T11:05:57.346","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-125323","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-11-10T18:17:33.703","lastModified":"2026-11-12T22:18:51.470","vulnStatus":"Deferred","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"pgEdge Control Plane is a distributed application for managing and orchestrating Postgres databases across multiple hosts. From 0.1.0 to 0.10.1, generated pg_hba.conf files began with hard-coded trust entries for Unix-socket and loopback connections. Because PostgreSQL evaluates the file from top to bottom, those entries also preempted operator-supplied rules in the pg_hba_conf field. Under the systemd orchestrator, any unprivileged operating-system account on a database host could authenticate as any PostgreSQL role, including the superuser, without credentials and obtain full control of the host's databases. Under Docker Swarm, reaching the container-local socket or loopback interface required code execution inside the database container. Publishing the PostgreSQL port to the host did not expose these trust rules because host connections did not appear to originate from 127.0.0.1 or ::1. This issue is fixed in version 0.11.0."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"pgEdge","product":"control-plane","versions":[{"version":"< 0.11.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"LOCAL","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":1.8,"impactScore":5.9}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:30:56.164483Z","id":"CVE-2026-125323","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-306"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-1188"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane/blob/main/changes/v0.11.0.md","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane/commit/88659f7388fc6c86125e60475aa83810171145b7","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane/pull/470","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane/releases/tag/v0.11.0","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane/security/advisories/GHSA-vq9p-w6wv-cr25","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-121876","sourceIdentifier":"secalert@redhat.com","published":"2026-11-12T17:17:29.040","lastModified":"2026-11-23T15:17:28.670","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"A flaw was found in the interaction between systemd-gpt-auto-generator and \nconfidential computing guest VM images in OpenShift Sandboxed Containers \n(confidential peer pods). systemd-gpt-auto-generator automatically discovers \nand mounts GPT partitions by type GUID at boot with no user confirmation. In \nthe confidential computing threat model, where the host/hypervisor is the \nadversary, a malicious host can inject partitions into the guest's virtual \ndisk. Most critically, injecting a swap partition causes the guest kernel to \npage out TEE-encrypted memory to a host-controlled block device, breaking the \nconfidentiality guarantee of the hardware TEE (AMD SEV-SNP, Intel TDX).\n\nThe PodVM images use a GPT-partitioned disk with dm-verity on the root \npartition. However, the roothash= kernel parameter only disables root \nauto-discovery — non-root partitions (swap, /home, /var, /srv, /var/tmp) are \nstill auto-discovered and mounted. The generator is shipped unmasked in the \nRHEL systemd-udev subpackage, and no kernel command line parameter in the \nmeasured UKI addon disables it. Additionally, the PodVM measurement script \ncaptures PCRs 3, 9, 11, and 12, but not PCR 5 (GPT partition table), so \npartition table modifications are not detected by remote attestation."}],"affected":[{"source":"secalert@redhat.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.3"],"versions":[{"version":"0:6.12.0-264.19.1.el10_3","lessThan":"*","versionType":"rpm","status":"unaffected"}]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:6"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:7"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel-rt","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:7"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel-rt","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"kernel-rt","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-8","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-9","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 5","defaultStatus":"affected","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-9","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:5"]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"secalert@redhat.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N","baseScore":7.9,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"LOCAL","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"HIGH","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"CHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"NONE"},"exploitabilityScore":1.5,"impactScore":5.8}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:11:12.120584Z","id":"CVE-2026-121876","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"secalert@redhat.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-359"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:102168","source":"secalert@redhat.com"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-121876","source":"secalert@redhat.com"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2558210","source":"secalert@redhat.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-127143","sourceIdentifier":"cvd@cert.pl","published":"2026-11-18T13:17:25.153","lastModified":"2026-11-18T21:17:48.033","vulnStatus":"Received","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"LMS (Lan Management System) is vulnerable to privilege escalation in the lmsd daemon. The daemon loads the libraries listed in the LMS database without checking that they come from a trusted location. An attacker with access to the web server process or with write access to the LMS database can register a malicious library and trigger a configuration reload, causing lmsd to load and execute it. Because the example systemd unit does not set a separate user, lmsd runs as root, allowing the attacker to execute arbitrary code with root privileges.\nThis issue was fixed in commit 89dd3f7. The lmsd component was removed. For existing installations that use lmsd, the recommended solution is to disable and remove this component."}],"affected":[{"source":"cvd@cert.pl","affectedData":[{"vendor":"LMS","product":"LMS","defaultStatus":"unaffected","modules":["lmsd"],"repo":"https://github.com/chilek/lms","versions":[{"version":"0","lessThan":"89dd3f7","versionType":"git","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV40":[{"source":"cvd@cert.pl","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"4.0","vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/R